{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1567, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given a simple undirected graph with N vertices and M edges, where the vertices are labeled 1 to N. The i-th edge connects vertices u_i and v_i.\r\nWhat is the minimum number of edges that need to be deleted from this graph so that the graph becomes a forest?\n\nWhat is a forest?\r\n\r\nA simple undirected graph F is called a forest if and only if F does not contain any cycle.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN M\r\nu_1 v_1\r\nu_2 v_2\r\n\\vdots\r\nu_M v_M\n\nOutput\n\nPrint the answer.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 1 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\times 10^5\n- 0 \\leq M \\leq \\min \\left( \\frac{N(N-1)}{2}, 2 \\times 10^5\\right)\n- 1 \\leq u_i < v_i \\leq N\n- The given graph is simple.\n- All input values are integers.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n4 4\r\n1 2\r\n1 3\r\n2 4\r\n3 4\n\nSample Output 1\n\n1\r\n\nFor example, if you delete the first edge, the graph becomes a forest.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n5 0\n\nSample Output 2\n\n0\n\nSample Input 3\n\n10 10\r\n7 9\r\n4 6\r\n6 10\r\n2 5\r\n5 6\r\n5 9\r\n6 8\r\n4 8\r\n1 5\r\n1 4\n\nSample Output 3\n\n2\n\n### Format: Read the inputs from stdin solve the problem and write the answer to stdout (do not directly test on the sample inputs). Enclose your code within delimiters as follows. Ensure that when the python program runs, it reads the inputs, runs the algorithm and writes output to STDOUT.\n```python\n# YOUR CODE HERE\n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1615, "char_start": 1579, "quote": "Input:\n4 4\n1 2\n1 3\n2 4\n3 4\nOutput:\n1", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1647, "char_start": 1627, "quote": "Input:\n5 0\nOutput:\n0", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R5", "source": {"char_end": 1722, "char_start": 1659, "quote": "Input:\n10 10\n7 9\n4 6\n6 10\n2 5\n5 6\n5 9\n6 8\n4 8\n1 5\n1 4\nOutput:\n2", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 3: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "a3b97f89b99f3f22042f63268654dcf5c215dde1d3b318f51eb98cb1e6e3dedb", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "6487daf0b2cf7d6362aa2cfd5d441ab16565cdbac31775dafc5bedee8ca8be71", "seq": 2}
